BEGIN:VCALENDAR
VERSION:2.0
PRODID:-//Littoralicious//Terroir Beaune//EN
X-WR-CALNAME:Beaune — eat & drink checklist
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:beaune-liste-1@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Œufs en meurette — Eggs poached in a reduction of red wine with lardons\, mushrooms and small onions\, on a garlic croûton.
DESCRIPTION:Say: uh ahn muh-RET. The plate where the wine is the sauce\, not the pairing. Best: Le Bistrot Bourguignon\, rue Monge — the first course
LOCATION:Le Bistrot Bourguignon\, rue Monge — the first course
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Le+Bistrot+Bourguignon+8+rue+Monge+Beaune+France
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:beaune-liste-2@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Bœuf bourguignon — Beef shoulder braised for hours in red wine until the sauce is dark and glossy.
DESCRIPTION:Say: buhf boor-gee-NYON. Built on the village wine that was never going to sell as cru. Best: Le Bistrot Bourguignon\, rue Monge
LOCATION:Le Bistrot Bourguignon\, rue Monge
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Le+Bistrot+Bourguignon+8+rue+Monge+Beaune+France
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:beaune-liste-3@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Jambon persillé — Ham simmered with white wine and herbs\, torn and set in parsley jelly\, sliced thick.
DESCRIPTION:Say: zhahm-BON pair-see-YAY. Burgundy’s Easter terrine\, sold all year on rue Monge. Best: Charcuterie Raillard\, 4 rue Monge — by the slice
LOCATION:Charcuterie Raillard\, 4 rue Monge — by the slice
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Charcuterie+Raillard+4+rue+Monge+Beaune+France
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:beaune-liste-4@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Pâté en croûte — Meat terrine baked inside a pastry crust\, served cold in slices.
DESCRIPTION:Say: pah-TAY ahn KROOT. The charcutier’s showpiece\; a whole one travels well to a galley. Best: Charcuterie Raillard\, rue Monge
LOCATION:Charcuterie Raillard\, rue Monge
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Charcuterie+Raillard+4+rue+Monge+Beaune+France
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:beaune-liste-5@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Escargots de Bourgogne — Snails baked in their shells under garlic and parsley butter.
DESCRIPTION:Say: es-kar-GOH duh boor-GOYN. Ask where the snails come from: the wild Burgundy snail is protected\, and most are imported. Best: Charcuterie Raillard\, rue Monge — escargots persillés to bake aboard
LOCATION:Charcuterie Raillard\, rue Monge — escargots persillés to bake aboard
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Charcuterie+Raillard+4+rue+Monge+Beaune+France
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:beaune-liste-6@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Époisses — A soft cow’s-milk cheese with an orange rind washed in brine and marc.
DESCRIPTION:Say: ay-PWAHSS. Made again at Époisses since the 1950s\; eat it ripe\, with a spoon. Best: Fromagerie Alain Hess\, Place Carnot\, or the Saturday market
LOCATION:Fromagerie Alain Hess\, Place Carnot\, or the Saturday market
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Fromagerie+Alain+Hess+7+Place+Carnot+Beaune+France
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:beaune-liste-7@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Cîteaux — A mild washed-rind cheese made by the Trappist monks of the Abbaye de Cîteaux.
DESCRIPTION:Say: see-TOH. The monks who walled the Clos de Vougeot still farm\; the cheese is sold at the abbey. Best: The Saturday market\, or the abbey shop at Cîteaux
LOCATION:The Saturday market\, or the abbey shop at Cîteaux
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Abbaye+de+Citeaux+France
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:beaune-liste-8@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Moutarde de Bourgogne — Mustard ground from Burgundy seed with white Burgundy wine\, under a protected name.
DESCRIPTION:Say: moo-TARD duh boor-GOYN. ‘Dijon’ on a jar is a method\; ‘de Bourgogne’ is a place. Best: Edmond Fallot\, 31 rue du Faubourg Bretonnière
LOCATION:Edmond Fallot\, 31 rue du Faubourg Bretonnière
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Edmond+Fallot+31+rue+du+Faubourg+Bretonniere+Beaune+France
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:beaune-liste-9@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Pain d’épices — Spice bread of flour and honey\, and the iced nonnettes made from it.
DESCRIPTION:Say: pan day-PEESS. Dijon’s bakers have made it since the eighteenth century. Best: Mulot & Petitjean\, Place Carnot
LOCATION:Mulot & Petitjean\, Place Carnot
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Mulot+et+Petitjean+Place+Carnot+Beaune+France
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:beaune-liste-10@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Beaune premier cru — A red Pinot Noir from one of the town’s 42 premier cru climats.
DESCRIPTION:Say: bohn pruh-MYAY KROO. Beaune has no grand cru: the premier crus are the top of its slope. Best: Marché aux Vins\, rue Nicolas Rolin — one is in the five-wine route
LOCATION:Marché aux Vins\, rue Nicolas Rolin — one is in the five-wine route
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Marche+aux+Vins+rue+Nicolas+Rolin+Beaune+France
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:beaune-liste-11@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Kir — Bourgogne Aligoté over a measure of crème de cassis\; a Kir Royale on Crémant.
DESCRIPTION:Say: KEER. Named for the canon who was mayor of Dijon from 1945 to 1968. Best: Mix it aboard: Aligoté and a Cassis de Dijon from the shops of the Place Carnot
LOCATION:Mix it aboard: Aligoté and a Cassis de Dijon from the shops of the Place Carnot
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Place+Carnot+Beaune+France
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:beaune-liste-12@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Crémant de Bourgogne — Burgundy’s sparkling wine\, made by a second fermentation in the bottle.
DESCRIPTION:Say: kray-MAHN duh boor-GOYN. An appellation since 1975\, at a fraction of the price of Champagne. Best: The Kir Royale’s base\; a bottle from Caves Madeleine’s shelves
LOCATION:The Kir Royale’s base\; a bottle from Caves Madeleine’s shelves
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Caves+Madeleine+8+rue+du+Faubourg+Madeleine+Beaune+France
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:beaune-liste-13@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Marc de Bourgogne — Brandy distilled from the pressed skins and pips after the harvest\, aged in wood.
DESCRIPTION:Say: mar duh boor-GOYN. Nothing of the harvest is wasted\; the Époisses rind is washed in it. Best: After dinner\, at Le Bistrot Bourguignon — ask for a Fine if you want it softer
LOCATION:After dinner\, at Le Bistrot Bourguignon — ask for a Fine if you want it softer
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Le+Bistrot+Bourguignon+8+rue+Monge+Beaune+France
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:beaune-liste-14@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Gougères — Warm choux puffs baked with cheese\, set out with the first glass.
DESCRIPTION:Say: goo-ZHAIR. The Côte’s way of opening a tasting\; no kept table lists them in 2026\, so take them where they are offered. Best: The Saturday market’s bakers and traiteurs (stalls vary)
LOCATION:The Saturday market’s bakers and traiteurs (stalls vary)
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Marche+de+Beaune+Place+de+la+Halle+Beaune+France
END:VTODO
END:VCALENDAR
